Three operator-approved pieces of work, one task, because all three touch the
fabrication gate or the capstone rot lint. Scope declared through
harness_integrity_lint with scripts/adversarial_verify.py unsealed by name.

Part A (REQ-SUBSTRATE-CLASS-1, REQ-SUBSTRATE-FREEZE-1). `inference_substrate` stays
prose. `inference_substrate_class` is a closed enum of seven values keyed to the
floors the gate already applies. The check lives in `_verify_artifact_impl`, which
the conductor's completion gate and the 24-hour backfill run; a hook is inert on
the population that widens the allowlists (29 of 30 widenings were conductor
commits). Absent class: WARN, only where the declared name matched no allowlist
and no name rule (973 of 6022 readable artifacts). A universal warn was measured
to break an existing empty-flag test on a real artifact. Present class: CRITICAL
on an out-of-enum value, a verdict contradiction, a typed-evidence contradiction,
or a duration below the class floor. Zero corpus artifacts carry the field. A
dict-shaped `inference_substrate` with no `value` is read as missing and warned;
measured on the 169 such artifacts: 0 critical added or removed. A pinned-length
test freezes the four alias tuples and the ARC floor table and names the one
duplicate (`cached_sota_event_energy_calibration`; 76 elements, 75 distinct).

Part B (REQ-VERIFY-7040, REQ-HARNESS-5945). The moat-rigor family reads `status`;
`moat_survives`, `beats_vote`, `beats_majority_vote` are claims; markers match on
a right token boundary (a left one rejected exp3923's `moatMOAT_SURVIVES`); null
markers take precedence; the SC token is matched on the full path; `MET_*` counts;
untuned and vanilla self-consistency are naive; `success_moat` is dropped so the
lint no longer quarantines its own receipt (exp5008). Corpus delta 14 artifacts,
all 2026-06/07, none stamped. Two decorative entries found by mutation were
removed. The capstone rot lint catches the sibling-raise shape, exempts recovery
helpers by mechanism (a git literal or a replay helper), and fails closed on an
unreadable module; the exemption is exercised on the V576, V580 and V598 helpers.

Part C. exp6847 (landed on hook-skipping conductor commit 89ed3aef60) refused on
the moved roadmap: 4 tests errored today and the lint refused the default glob.
Code fix: `_milestone_inputs` recovers roadmap and design from the commit that
held V598. exp5008: code fix for the false positive; the artifact and its stamp
are left as they are, an accepted state for an operator corrigendum.

Proof: 36 distinct mutations RED, all restored byte-identically, run unlocked in
the worktree with PYTHONPATH pinned and the imported paths printed. Three
survivors across two passes resolved by removing decorative entries and adding an
isolating test. Regression over 118 gate-reaching test files: 130 of 131 failures
reproduce with HEAD's gate swapped in (set difference empty), so they pre-exist;
the one that did not was this task's own test expectation, fixed.

Not done: CLAUDE.md (draft in the research note, Appendix A); the planner prompt;
any tuple widening; any edit under results/. Operator decisions are listed in the
note, section 8.

